{"nodes": [{"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_po_reroute", "label": "PO Reroute Workflow (v3)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_requirement_verbatim", "label": "Purchasings Verbatim Requirement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml:3-13", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "We dont want the AI improvising a PO reroute. The steps are fixed... In that order. Every time. The planner decides whether to enter the workflow and supplies parameters; it cannot reorder, skip or add a step, and never sees this file."}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_reversibility_ordering", "label": "Reversibility-Ordered Steps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml:18-25", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every compensable write comes before the one irreversible effect. Notify first, buy second would leave a supervisor acting on a PO that does not exist. Rollback safety is a property of the ordering, not only of the compensations."}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_bounded_model_steps", "label": "Bounded Model Steps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml:27-35", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "choose_supplier looks like the model making a purchasing decision but is not: code computed who is qualified and removed anyone too slow. The model picks among options code produced. Neither model step may write - the loader rejects an llm step that names a tool."}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_on_empty_fail", "label": "on_empty: fail Confirmation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml:62-65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What makes step 1 a confirmation rather than a lookup: no qualified supplier means there is no reroute to make, and the workflow stops instead of proceeding to invent one."}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_enum_from_guardrail", "label": "enum_from Guardrail", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml:89-93", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Permitted answers are computed at run time from step 2 output. A supplier outside that list fails the guardrail, is audited as a rejection, retried once, then fails the workflow closed."}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_must_mention_guardrail", "label": "must_mention Guardrail", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml:150-154", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Forces the drafted message to name the production order and the new purchase order. A notification about a supply change that never says which one is not a notification."}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_irreversible_declaration", "label": "Irreversible Step Declaration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml:186-190", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "irreversible: true rather than a missing compensation. The loader rejects a write that declares neither, so rollback is always a decision somebody made."}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_find_approved_suppliers", "label": "Step 1: Find Approved Suppliers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_filter_by_lead_time", "label": "Step 2: Filter By Lead Time", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_choose_supplier", "label": "Step 3: Choose Supplier (LLM)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_create_replacement_po", "label": "Step 4: Create Replacement PO", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_reduce_original_po", "label": "Step 5: Cancel Or Reduce Original PO", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_draft_notification", "label": "Step 6: Draft Notification (LLM)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "northfield/workflows/po_reroute.v3.yaml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "northfield_workflows_po_reroute_v3_notify_production", "label": "Step 7